  "id": "struggle-for-existence",
  "term": "struggle for existence",
  "definition": "In this historical source, the struggle for existence means competition among different groups, understood as a force that shapes economic types through natural selection. It is used to explain why laws about human economic motives apply only under the conditions that form and sustain those types.",
